<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 25 January, from 750 to 1971.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/750">750 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,276 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Abbasids defeat the Umayyads at the Battle of the Zab</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Abbasid rebels defeated the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> on the banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-zab">Great Zab</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. The battle spelled the end of the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> and the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a>, who ruled as caliphs until 1258.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1327">1327 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">699 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward III is proclaimed king of England in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After Queen Isabella and Roger Mortimer invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and summoned a parliament, King Edward II was forced to give up the throne, and his fourteen-year-old son was proclaimed king in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. He was crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a> on 1 February.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-ii-of-england">Edward II of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1533">1533 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">493 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII secretly marries Anne Boleyn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry married the pregnant Anne Boleyn in a private ceremony at Whitehall while still married to Catherine of Aragon. To make the marriage lawful he broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and headed his own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-england">Church of England</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1554">1554 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">472 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jesuit missionaries found São Paulo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-da-nobrega">Manuel da Nóbrega</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-anchieta">José de Anchieta</a> celebrated Mass at a new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> mission on the Piratininga plateau. The settlement grew into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a>, now the largest city in the Southern Hemisphere.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1858">1858 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">168 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria's eldest daughter marries Prince Frederick of Prussia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Victoria, the Princess Royal, married the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-emperor">German Emperor</a> Frederick III at St James's Palace. Mendelssohn's 'Wedding March' played as they left, starting a fashion for it at weddings.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1881">1881 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">145 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edison and Bell interests form the Oriental Telephone Company</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Companies holding the telephone patents of Thomas Edison and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell">Alexander Graham Bell</a> combined to form the Oriental Telephone Company. It built early telephone exchanges in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and other parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell">Alexander Graham Bell</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1924">1924 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">102 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Winter Olympics open at Chamonix</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An 'International Winter Sports Week' opened at Chamonix in the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> with athletes from 16 nations. The International Olympic Committee later recognised it as the first Winter Olympic Games.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of the Bulge ends in Allied victory</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Allied forces restored their line in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a>, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s last major offensive in the west. Fought in bitter winter conditions, it was the costliest American battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1971">1971 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">55 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Idi Amin seizes power in Uganda</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">While President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a> was abroad, army commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a> took power in a coup. His eight-year rule saw the expulsion of Uganda's Asians and the killing of an estimated 100,000 to 500,000 people.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 25 January <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leo-iv-the-khazar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leo-iv-the-khazar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leo IV the Khazar</span><span class="tp">750–780</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-brittany"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anne-of-brittany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anne of Brittany</span><span class="tp">1477–1514</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/paul-henri-spaak"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/paul-henri-spaak.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Paul-Henri Spaak</span><span class="tp">1899–1972</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/janio-quadros"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/janio-quadros.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jânio Quadros</span><span class="tp">1917–1992</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eduard-shevardnadze"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eduard-shevardnadze.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eduard Shevardnadze</span><span class="tp">1928–2014</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/corazon-aquino"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/corazon-aquino.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Corazon Aquino</span><span class="tp">1933–2009</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 25 January <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/antipope-anacletus-ii"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Antipope Anacletus II</span><span class="tp">d. 1138</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/godfrey-i-of-louvain"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/godfrey-i-of-louvain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Godfrey I of Louvain</span><span class="tp">c. 1060–1139</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-duke-of-lorraine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-ii-duke-of-lorraine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles II, Duke of Lorraine</span><span class="tp">1364–1431</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christian-ii-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christian-ii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christian II of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1481–1559</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
